WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's been such a great year
for you

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
since the last time
you were here.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
You won the Emmy,
you won the Golden Globe,

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but on Saturday,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had one of the biggest
things happen.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:11.011 size:88% position:44%
You were impersonated on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And Cecily Strong did you.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:17.017
And here is Aidy Bryant
as Amy Sherman-Palladino.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.419 line:92%
And you tweeted about it.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:21.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
You seemed very --
Were you very excited?

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I still feel that way.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm still making that face.
Just...

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.294 size:78% position:39%
-And so, you did not
see it live, correct?

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
Someone else --
-No. I was abroad,

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.698 line:92%
and so I was six hours ahead.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:35.335
And everyone I have ever met
had sent me a text message

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the time I woke up
the next morning.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.172 size:75% position:38%
-And then, do you go
into it with nerves?

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, obviously, people
get impersonated on it.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.810 size:88% position:44%
This was done with love.
Sometimes they're not.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Other people were tweeting
about "SNL" this week,

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:49.382
and they were less happy.
-They were not so thrilled about
that, yeah.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
No. I mean, even if
it had been terrible,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like I still
would have been thrilled.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.557
-That's great.
That is right way to go into it.

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the coolest things
about season two

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.728 size:78% position:39% line:92%
is it opens in Paris,

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is not
sound stage Paris.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys actually
got to go to Paris.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.234 size:88% position:44%
I mean, was that just so
exciting to shoot there?

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:13.106
-It was amazing and so strange
to start the season that way.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:13.673 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-New York is a character
in the show.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:19.612
And so, to begin season two in
Paris, we were very confused.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it was amazing.
We ate all the baguettes.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
We drank all the wine.
-Yeah.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.919 line:92%
-And we had a great time.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like "Maisel" camp
in Paris.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.222 line:92%
-You got to shoot a scene

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:32.358
where you were doing stand-up
and you had a French translator.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
What -- How --
That was also fantastic.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.596 size:78% position:39%
-Wasn't she amazing?
-She was great, yeah.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.564 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-She was so talented.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
She came in for this --
She was actually --

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
She got the job because
she did such a beautiful job

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.771 size:78% position:39%
just reading the part
at the table read.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.738 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And she jumped in.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:49.175
And I didn't think there were
very many people out there

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.777 line:92%
who can speak as fast as I can,

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
but Leslie gave me
a run for my money.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
In another language no less.

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

